# MOVEMENT IV — file 73: b97-144 = DEVELOPMENT.
# [G] b97-108  CELL vs its AUGMENTATION, p.  vc+cb walk the CELL in
#     staccato quarters (CELL4) round the circle of fifths Cm - Fm - Bb -
#     Eb - Ab - (Ger6) - G; above each 2-bar unit a single voice spins the
#     P head (CELL in 8ths + rising scale bar): vn1, ob1, vn1, fl1+cl1,
#     vn1+ob (+fl 8va, cresc), all strings+winds on G MAJOR (mf) - the
#     CELL in major heard for the first time, a promise of the coda.
# [H] b109-124 FUGATO.  Subject = CELL4 on i + CELL4 on v (4 bars of
#     quarters); countersubject = the P head in 8ths (which is the same
#     CELL, diminished).  When the CS lies BELOW the subject its 7th 8th
#     slides down a semitone (g-f#-f-d) to avoid a 9th against the bass.
#     Entries: vc/cb/fg (Cm) b109, va+cl1 (Gm) b113, vn2+ob (Cm) b117,
#     vn1+fl (Gm, 2nd half on D major) b121; f -> cresc.
# [I] b125-132 The head of Mvt-I theme T1 (d-g ... bb-a-g-f#-d), in
#     half-note augmentation = its original speed, ff in vn1+fl+ob (+cl
#     8vb) over CELL L5 in the basses and the P head in vn2; G minor,
#     then a 4th higher in C minor, Phrygian cadence (Cm/Eb - D) onto:
# [J] b133-144 DOMINANT PEDAL D.  b133-136 ff arpeggios over D, Cm/D,
#     dim7/D, D7; b137-140 the CELL on D sinks vn1 -> vn2 -> va -> vc,
#     dim.; b141-142 pp, the CELL alone in vc/cb; b143-144 cresc, scale
#     climbing in vn1/vn2/va into the recapitulation.

